Subject: [202605] Remove Debian pycparser before installing VS runtime wheels

The inherited image contains Debian pycparser 2.21, but VS runtime constraints
select pycparser 3.0. Pip cannot uninstall the distutils-managed Debian package.
Remove it using apt before the wheel installation, preserving upstream pins.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/issues/30609
Precedent: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/1820
Verified source: 8076a44fa579fde75f73299f03e7f3cac298d9e3.
Remove once upstream handles Debian/pip package ownership in this image.

--- a/platform/vs/docker-sonic-vs/Dockerfile.j2
+++ b/platform/vs/docker-sonic-vs/Dockerfile.j2
@@ -106,6 +106,9 @@
 # Copy locally-built Python wheel dependencies
 {{ copy_files("python-wheels/", docker_sonic_vs_whls.split(' '), "/python-wheels/") }}
 
+# Remove the Debian-owned distutils package before pip installs pinned pycparser.
+RUN apt-get remove -y python3-pycparser
+
 # Install locally-built Python wheel dependencies
 {{ install_python_wheels(docker_sonic_vs_whls.split(' ')) }}
 {% endif %}
